    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0671" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1949v02/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/7–2049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Venezuela </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-21T18:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>263. Latest reports in Guat indicate fighting between followers of Arana, who was
                    Chief of Armed Forces,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d397-f1"/> on one hand and those of
                    President and Minister of National Defense<anchor n="2" xml:id="d397-f2"/> on
                    the other, ceased late Tues<anchor n="3" xml:id="d397-f3"/> (urtel 457<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d397-f4"/>). Good offices dipl corps instrumental preventing
                    prolongation fighting. No casualties Amer citizens reported. General situation
                    now calm.</p>
                <p>Fighting by Arana followers apparently lacking in plan and coordination and
                    probably resulted as spontaneous reaction assassination and arrest certain Arana
                    supporters. Whole incident seems instigated by Army elements allied with PAR and
                    other radical groups to prevent Arana from gaining full control Army fol
                    successful election last week of additional Arana supporters to Supreme War
                    Council. <pb facs="0672" n="656" xml:id="pg656"/> Overall result appears signify
                    defeat of moderate elements govt and substantial strengthening leftists.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d397-f1" n="1" xml:id="d397-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Francisco Arana, Chief of the Guatemalan Armed Forces, had been assassinated
                    in Guatemala on July 18.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d397-f2" n="2" xml:id="d397-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Jacobo Arbenz Guzmán.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d397-f3" n="3" xml:id="d397-f3-content">
                <p>July 19, 1949.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d397-f4" n="4" xml:id="d397-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested information on the assassination and outbreak of
                    fighting in Guatemala.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
